2c107596 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #Yes—using built-in Find and Replace:
2c107596 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c107596 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #1. Open Replace with `Ctrl+H` (`Cmd+Option+F` on macOS).
2c107596 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #2. Enable Use Regular Expression (the `.*` button).
2c107597 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #3. In Find, enter:
2c107597 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #   `^\s*\n`
2c107597 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #4. Leave Replace empty.
2c107598 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #5. Click Replace All.
2c107598 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c107598 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #This removes empty lines and lines containing only whitespace. To remove only completely empty
2c107598 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #lines, use `^\r?\n` instead.
2c107599 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c108e65 [nitro@ryzen5] what is overton window?
2c108fc0 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 kimi-k3.1-pro 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.006 1.093KB 21.18s
2c108fc1 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #The Overton window is the range of ideas or policies considered socially and
2c108fc1 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #politically acceptable at a particular time. Ideas inside the window can be debated seriously;
2c108fc2 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #ideas outside it are viewed as extreme, radical, or unthinkable.
2c108fc3 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c108fc3 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #It is named after Joseph Overton, who argued that politicians generally support only
2c108fc4 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #policies they believe voters will accept. A common scale is:
2c108fc4 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c108fc4 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #• Unthinkable → Radical → Acceptable → Sensible → Popular → Policy*
2c108fc5 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c108fc6 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #The window can move or widen over time because of social movements, media coverage,
2c108fc6 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #advocacy, crises, or changing public values. For example, an idea initially dismissed as radical
2c108fc6 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #may gradually become mainstream and eventually be enacted into law. Ideas can also move in the
2c108fc7 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #opposite direction.
2c108fc7 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c108fc7 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #The Overton window is about public acceptability, not whether an idea is morally right,
2c108fc7 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #effective, or already legal. It can also differ between countries, communities, and political
2c108fc8 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #groups. Sometimes people introduce more extreme proposals partly to make other proposals seem
2c108fc9 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #moderate by comparison, though shifts in the window are not always deliberate.
2c108fc9 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
