2c10f250 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 kimi-k3.1-pro 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.005 4.511KB 21.38s
2c10f251 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #No. “All rights reserved” means the copyright holder retains the rights granted by
2c10f251 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #copyright law. A license then grants others specific permissions—such as copying, modifying, and
2c10f251 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #redistributing—subject to its terms.
2c10f251 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c10f252 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #So the header effectively means:
2c10f252 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c10f252 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #	imon Armstrong retains copyright; everyone else may use the work under the Apache 2.0 license.
2c10f252 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c10f253 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #The phrase is largely redundant in modern copyright law, but it remains conventional. It would
2c10f253 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #conflict only with a dedication that surrendered copyright entirely, not with an ordinary
2c10f253 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #open-source license. If your module uses a license other than Apache 2.0, the header should name
2c10f253 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #that license instead.
2c10f253 [kimi-k3.1-pro] #
2c10f254 [roha] imon Armstrong retains copyright; everyone else may use the work under the Apache 2.0 license.
